# The certificate request (core/der.h builds it, adapters/certificate_authority/request.rs reads it). `tbs` is the part that is
# signed, built from name, spki and challenge (the channel binding as base64, or none); `signature` is a real ECDSA P-256 /
# SHA-256 signature over it, made once with OpenSSL (README.md here); `request` is the finished request.
# The display must build `tbs` and `request` byte for byte; the server must read the name, the key and the binding from `request`
# and accept its signature. `binding` is the challenge decoded, as hex, or none.

